    /// Themes ported from `packages/web/packages/themes/src/styles/*.css` so the
    /// Swift and web catalogues match. These are brand themes with no ANSI
    /// palette of their own: `ansi` is derived from their semantic colours as a
    /// best-effort fill for the terminal feature, while `roleOverrides` carries
    /// the exact web values that drive chat and `typography` carries each
    /// theme's `--pc-font` / `--font-mono` stack.
    ///
    /// Generated by `scripts/generate_web_theme_swift.py` from
    /// `scripts/extract_web_themes.py`'s output — do not hand-edit; re-run the
    /// generator instead. See `olyloapp/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-30-swift-chat-parity.md`,
    /// Task 4.
    ///
    /// 21 of the manifest's 39 keys. The `adh*` font-variant family (8) is
    /// absent because those share one palette and differ only in typography, a
    /// web font-loading concern with no Swift analogue; the ten editor palettes
    /// (dracula, nord, gruvbox, solarized, catppuccin, github, monokai,
    /// one-dark, tokyo-night, rose-pine) are absent because Swift already
    /// ships them as terminal themes with real ANSI palettes — porting the web
    /// copies would give us two of each, and the web copy would be the worse
    /// one.
